# Copy to .env.production (or .env) and fill in real values for a Vercel
# deployment. Vite bakes VITE_-prefixed vars into the built bundle at BUILD
# time - set these as Vercel project Environment Variables instead of a
# committed file. Leave unset for normal local dev (see dashboard.js's
# fallback) - none of this is needed to just run `npm run dev`.
#
# NOTE: /api/* and /play/* requests are NOT configured here - they need
# rewrites in vercel.json pointing at the real backend/client respectively
# (see that file's own comment, and client/vite.config.js's `base`), since
# Vite's dev-only server.proxy (vite.config.js) has no effect on a
# production build at all.

# Leave this UNSET in the normal/recommended setup - dashboard.js's own
# fallback ('/play') already routes through vercel.json's rewrite to the
# client, keeping the whole flow (dashboard through live match) on this
# same origin so an installed "Add to Home Screen" PWA stays in standalone
# mode all the way through (a different origin drops it back into normal
# browser chrome the instant you navigate there - see dashboard.js's own
# comment on GAME_CLIENT_URL for the full story). Only set this to the
# client's own separate domain, e.g. https://wrag-fps-client.vercel.app/,
# if that reverse-proxy setup genuinely isn't possible for your deployment.
VITE_GAME_CLIENT_URL=
